<title>ITALY: ALPINE SKIING-ZURBRIGGEN AND KOSTNER WIN DOWNHILL.</title>
<headline>ALPINE SKIING-ZURBRIGGEN AND KOSTNER WIN DOWNHILL.</headline>
<dateline>CORTINA D'AMPEZZO, Italy 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Switzerland's Heidi Zurbriggen and Italy's Isolde Kostner shared victory in a women's World Cup Alpine skiing downhill on Friday, according to provisional results.</p>
<p>Both skiers clocked one minute 30.81 seconds. In one of the closest finishes ever, Germany's Katja Seizinger was third just two hundredths of a second behind in 1:30.83.</p>
</text>
